<A HREF="/msnmain?fn=130&fmt=hl&pg1=IID&s1=120898&v1=Klimyk%2C%20A%2E%20U%2E">Klimyk, A. U.</A><A HREF="/msnmain?fn=505&pg1=CODE&s1=UKR_AOS_TP&v1=UKR-AOS-TP">(UKR-AOS-TP)</A>
<BR>
<strong> Kravchuk polynomials and group representation.
</strong> <STRONG>(Ukrainian. Russian, Ukrainian summary)</STRONG>
 <A HREF="/msnmain?fn=305&pg1=CN&s1=Ukrain_Mat_Zh&v1=Ukra%5C%22%5Ci%20n%2E%20Mat%2E%20Zh%2E"><EM> Ukra&iuml;n. Mat. Zh. </EM></A><STRONG> 44 </STRONG> (1992), <A HREF="/msnmain?fn=130&pg1=ISSI&s1=120725&v1=Ukrainian%20Mathematical%20Journal%20%5B%2044%20%281992%29%2Cno%2E%207%5D"> no. 7,</A>888--901; <EM> translation in </EM><A HREF="/msnmain?fn=305&pg1=CN&s1=Ukrainian_Math_J&v1=Ukrainian%20Math%2E%20J%2E"> <EM>Ukrainian Math. J.</EM></A> <STRONG> 44 </STRONG> (1992), <A HREF="/msnmain?fn=130&pg1=ISSI&s1=124206&v1=Ukrainian%20Mathematical%20Journal%20%5B%2044%20%281992%29%2C%20no%2E%207%5D"> no. 7,</A> 801--812 (1993)  <BR CLEAR=RIGHT>
<HR NOSHADE SIZE="1">Krawtchouk [Kravchuk] polynomials form a system of orthogonal polynomials in a
discrete variable with a weight function describing the binomial
probability distribution. The paper presents a survey of connections
of Krawtchouk polynomials, as well as of their different
$q$-analogues, with the representation theory of groups. The paper
describes general relations between the theory of special functions
and group representations. Concrete expressions are given both for
Krawtchouk polynomials through hypergeometric functions and for
different types of Krawtchouk $q$-polynomials through basic
hypergeometric functions (or $q$-hypergeometric functions). The
connections of Krawtchouk polynomials and Krawtchouk-Meixner functions
with the representations of ${\rm SU}(2)$, the symmetric group, the
quantum group ${\rm SU}\sb q(2)$ and the Chevalley groups are described.<P><P>
